---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../../../components/docs/Callout.astro';
import Code from '../../../components/docs/Code.astro';
import DeviceConstraints from '../../../components/docs/DeviceConstraints.astro';
import { page } from '../../../data/docs-nav';

const entry = page('/docs/destinations/mac/');

const probe = `# Point a browser or curl at the Mac, on the same network:
curl http://your-mac.local:54330/

{"service":"hozz-receiver","ready":true,"name":"Brandon's Mac"}`;
---

<DocsLayout page={entry} section="Destinations">
  <div class="fact-strip">
    <div>
      <dt>Format</dt>
      <dd>NDJSON</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Port</dt>
      <dd>54330</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Needs</dt>
      <dd>Both devices on one network</dd>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    The Mac app receives batches over your network, stores them in SQLite, charts them, and serves
    them through <a href="/docs/mcp/">MCP</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Setting it up</h2>

  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      <h3>Open Hozz on the Mac</h3>
      <p>
        It listens on <strong>54330</strong> and advertises <code>_hozz._tcp</code>.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>On the iPhone, add a destination</h3>
      <p>
        Pick it under <strong>Your computers</strong>.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Test it</h3>
      <p>
        Hozz fills the address and token. Use <strong>Send a test</strong>.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>How the phone finds the Mac</h2>

  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Bonjour:</strong> the normal path.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>iCloud Keychain:</strong> when available, it can sync the pairing token between
      devices on one Apple ID.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Local sweep:</strong> a private <code>/24</code> on port 54330 when mDNS fails.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Authentication</h2>

  <p>
    Deliveries require an <code>Authorization</code> token. <code>GET /</code> and{' '}
    <code>POST /pair</code> are unauthenticated. Wrong or missing delivery tokens return{' '}
    <code>401</code>.
  </p>

  <p>
    A <code>GET</code> identifies the receiver:
  </p>

  <Code caption="Checking the receiver is up" code={probe} />

  <Callout kind="note" title="Already paired with another device">
    <p>
      A paired Mac returns <code>403</code>: <em
        >This Mac is already paired with another device. Open Hozz on the Mac and forget it first,
        or copy the token by hand.</em
      >
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>If the local network will not cooperate</h2>

  <p>
    Guest, isolated and corporate networks may block device-to-device traffic. Use the folder
    watcher instead.
  </p>

  <p>
    Point both apps at the same synced <a href="/docs/destinations/folder/">folder</a>. The Mac
    ingests NDJSON, JSON, CSV and Metrics JSON.
  </p>

  <h2>What the Mac app does with it</h2>

  <p>Received batches go into <code>hozz-received.sqlite</code>.</p>

  <p>The app has four tabs:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Connect</strong> — the receiver, the folder watcher, the token, and per-device status based on when data last actually arrived.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Data</strong> — coverage, characteristics, charts and CSV export.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Assistant</strong> — the MCP configuration to copy into an assistant.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Activity</strong> — accepted, duplicate, paired, test and rejected deliveries.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <Callout kind="note" title="Quarantine, and why nothing is dropped">
    <p>
      Unknown records are quarantined and named in Data. A later version can promote them.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>A dependency-free alternative</h2>

  <p>
    A dependency-free Python receiver lives in <code>receiver/</code>.{' '}
    <a href="/docs/destinations/web/">Your own endpoint</a> documents the protocol.
  </p>

  <DeviceConstraints />
</DocsLayout>
